[00:23.80]1. O God, you know my rest and waking,
[00:31.02]When I lie down and when I rise anew.
[00:38.59]You search my thoughts, my inmost inclination,
[00:46.27]The words I speak, the ways I walk,
[00:49.95]you know them too.
[00:54.24]You saw when I was made in secret,
[01:01.74]My very bones not hidden from your sight.
[01:09.40]You saw my form; its parts were down in writing.
[01:16.84]I love the wonder of your ways
[01:20.71]and praise your might.
[01:24.57]Your knowledge, God, is wondrous, awe-inspiring;
[01:31.57]Of this my soul is very well-aware.
[01:39.64]If I should fear that darkness might enfold me,
[01:46.70]Your spirit, God, would find me, even there.
[01:54.68]Where could I hide from you, Jehovah,
[02:02.40]Or be concealed, be hidden from your face?
[02:09.40]Not in the Grave nor in the highest heaven,
[03:17.96]Not in the dark nor in the sea;
[03:31.47]there is no place.